## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook **"coverage theater"** suite. Every production method is called (→ 95% coverage), but almost nothing is actually **verified**. Here's the severity-ranked breakdown:

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — No assertions at all (tests can never fail)

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)** — Fire-and-forget. Never checks the product was stored.
```csharp
// Fix: verify the round-trip
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var saved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", saved?.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, saved?.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)** — Calls `UpdatePrice` but never reads the result back.
```csharp
// Fix: verify the price actually changed
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 39)** — Calls `RemoveProduct` but never confirms deletion.
```csharp
// Fix: verify product is gone
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)** — Doesn't even add data, and never asserts the count.
```csharp
// Fix: add products and verify the count
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(2, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)** — Applies 10% discount but never checks prices changed. A broken discount formula would pass green.
```csharp
// Fix: verify discounted prices
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")?.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")?.Price);
```

**6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85)** — Imports data, never checks it was parsed/stored.
```csharp
// Fix: verify imported product
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var p = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", p?.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, p?.Price);
```

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Weak assertions (assert something, but not the right thing)

**7. `GetProduct_Works` (line 23)** — Asserts `IsNotNull` but never checks the returned values. Could return the wrong product and still pass.
